ust keep it small and we can meet  up in the spring you know easter can be  the new christmas for some people well i  mean many people  many people will hear that and see a  strong suggestion from the housing  secretary that actually guys  maybe you don't want to do christmas do  you understand there are conflicting  messages this is fine for you to say  no i think because the decision the  difference between the difference  between us with respect is that you want  the government to tell everybody what  they should be doing at christmas  and my view is that the government can  set a legal framework  and then it's for people to use their  good judgment you can't legislate for  every eventuality  particularly something as sensitive as  christmas where people will come  to different judgments based on the  vulnerabilities of their own family  and how important this is to them  because there are many people as i say  who have been longing to get together  at the end of a very long and difficult  year and i think we have to respect the  fact that people will come to different  conclusions can you  then give us an update as to how the  vaccination program is going we have  figures for scotland  we have figures for northern ireland we  don't have figures for england again and  and once again we hear reports from  doctors  from gp surgeries that they are adding  doing numbers  ultimately almost essentially on the  back of a fact packet  they're using scrap bits of paper to try  to come to totals why do we not yet have  a total for england  well we will do soon but we're going to  do it in a in a  um a sensible way when we've got  the data together it's properly verified  then we'll publish it we certainly don't  want to be publishing  data that we're not a hundred percent  confident of  we have rolled out tens of thousands of  vaccines a very large quantity of course  as you know  we are the most advanced coach in the  world at rolling out a medically  efficacious vaccine 